Z||000003||Smoooooth GT||06-06-2001||12:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cadaver:<BR><B>Whats it from. I have a garret T3 liquid cooled that Im playing with.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>that's the same turbo that I'm playing with.. the Garrett T-3 .65ar liquid cooled also.  Chris West is supposed to be working on making me my crossover pipe. the only thing left that I have to get is the rising regulator, and the crossover before I start to do all the plumbing of the oil and cooling lines. I've been putting all of my time and $ into the body work I'm doing on the Smooth GT.... <P>------------------<BR>aka..FieroSEt<BR>Fiero_87GT@yahoo.com<BR>cell.. 903 445 0849<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_6.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||BV MotorSports||06-06-2001||12:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by The Fieromaster:<BR><B>I was walking around the local yard a few weeks ago and found a turbo so I purchased it it turns out to be a pretty evil turbo... It is an IHI RHB5.  Its nice its LIQUID cooled   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> turbo! Woo Hoo!  So now im wondering does anyone have turbo experience.. I want this thing in my car!!!  Thanks to you all if you can help   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats a pretty big turbo for a 2.8! If it is a 393B trim it is recomended for small to med sized V8 with a 5000rpm limit and approx 481 cfm @ 7 psi.<BR>It shows it can be used on a 4cyl if your max rpm is 7000  in the 311A trim.<P>shows 393A trim can be used on a v6 w/ 6500 rpm limit.<BR>Either show a max RPM of 10,000 so I doubt you will ever hit that.<P>I have a illistration of that turbo complete with compressor map if you would like. I could scan it and e-mail it to you. Shows all mount flange sizez and everything!<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||06-06-2001||06:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BV MotorSports:<BR><B> Thats a pretty big turbo for a 2.8! <BR>Steven<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Big? They came on the four cylinder fords. I think they were 3.4 or around there.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Smoooooth GT:<BR><B> I have to get is the rising regulator, and the crossover before I start to do all the plumbing </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Why use a rising rate regulator. You will need a 1BAR map sensor and burn a chip for the ecm. The earlier ECM have an easier time with turbos. You will also need some way to retard the timing under boost conditions. Like a MSD 6BTM<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||The Fieromaster||06-07-2001||03:50 AM||||yea i planned on buying an ignition system that has a boost retard... $$$ Im not tooo worried about cause i can do all the metal working myself casue im cool like that (LOL) as for ecm chip... oh yea i cant wait.. lol!  I also am lookin at a electronic boost controller with scramble and a sweet LOUD bov 150+ decibles hehe!!  Im gonna mount all the controls (boost, ingitions, and some warning lights) where the GT gauges SHOULD go in the factory GT pod but with a custom face so it all fits nice and flush... Im gonna TRY to contact Steve Hamm (SP) about making me some manifolds (for some nice $$) cause he did his on his EVIL EVIL EVIL 320+ hp 2.8 turbo.. fastest thing ive ever seen!  But im not sure if he is on this list.. although he lives like 2 cities away!  If anyone knows him can ya let him know id like to get ahold of him!  Thanks!<P>--- Oh yea ----<BR>Bv motorsports... it is the 4 banger one because I do have the origanal manifold for it (one heavy mo fo too) id be VERY gratfull if you could send that scan to fieromaster@ncweb.com thanks soo much!!<BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">    <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000<p>[This message has been edited by The Fieromaster (edited 06-07-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000007||BBBAD GT||06-07-2001||09:03 AM||||Sounds like its off a 1987-88 Ford Thunderbird Turbo Coupe.  They had liquid cooled IHI turbos (PN 1H1RHB-52 turbo with integral waste gate), and are not bad turbos.  They top out at 15lb of boost with the 2.3L 4cyl motor, and are not that efficent above that.  They do spool a little quicker than the T3's that are found in the Mustang SVO's, but they are capable of around 18-19lb of boost.  I bought a used TC motor and sold the IHI turbo on Ebay just recently.  Some pics are at: <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/parts/turbo1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/parts/turbo1.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/parts/turbo2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/parts/turbo2.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/parts/turbo3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/parts/turbo3.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/parts/turbo4.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/parts/turbo4.jpg</A> <BR>Go to the Thunderbird Turbo Coupe's web sites and get some more info about this turbo.<P>BTW, what are you going to do with the manifold?  What PN is on it (does it start with E6?).  I'd be interested in it if its not cracked (the older E3 manifolds are prone to cracking, the E6's weren't).<P><BR>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">         <P>86 Mustang SVO<P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A><p>[This message has been edited by BBBAD GT (edited 06-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||gabriel||06-07-2001||10:39 AM||||Yep, that's the turbo thats in my 88 T-Bird coupe.  Very nice item ... if you want to try more boost you will have to modify the fixed wastegate.  Let us know how it all turns out||||reg||1
